    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-191",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "191 Director, producer and screenwriter of cinematograph film",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-191"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A reference in this Part to the director of a cinematograph film in\nthe direction of which 2 or more individuals were involved is a\nreference to the principal director of the film and does not include a\nreference to any subsidiary director, whether described as an\nassociate director, line director, assistant director or in any other\nway.\n\n(2) A reference in this Part to the producer of a cinematograph film is\na reference to:\n\n(a) the individual who was the producer of the film; or\n\n(b) if there were 2 or more individuals involved in the production\nof the film—the individual who was the principal producer of\nthe film;\nand does not include a reference to any subsidiary producer,\nwhether described as an executive producer, associate producer,\nline producer, assistant producer or in any other way.\n\nSchedule 1  Moral rights of authors\n\n(3) As only individuals have moral rights (see section 190), if the\nproducer of a cinematograph film was a body corporate, the only\nmoral rights in respect of the film are those of the director and\nscreenwriter.\n\n(4) A reference in this Part to the screenwriter of a cinematograph film\nfor which 2 or more individuals were involved in the writing of the\nscript or screenplay is a reference to the principal screenwriter.\nNote:\nIf there were 2 or more principal directors, 2 or more individuals who\nwere the principal producers, or 2 or more principal screenwriters, of a\ncinematograph film, section 195AZJ, 195AZK or 195AZL applies.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A reference in this Part to the director of a cinematograph film in\nthe direction of which 2 or more individuals were involved is a\nreference to the principal director of the film and does not include a\nreference to any subsidiary director, whether described as an\nassociate director, line director, assistant director or in any other\nway.\n\n(2) A reference in this Part to the producer of a cinematograph film is\na reference to:\n\n(a) the individual who was the producer of the film; or\n\n(b) if there were 2 or more individuals involved in the production\nof the film—the individual who was the principal producer of\nthe film;\nand does not include a reference to any subsidiary producer,\nwhether described as an executive producer, associate producer,\nline producer, assistant producer or in any other way.\n\nSchedule 1  Moral rights of authors\n\n(3) As only individuals have moral rights (see section 190), if the\nproducer of a cinematograph film was a body corporate, the only\nmoral rights in respect of the film are those of the director and\nscreenwriter.\n\n(4) A reference in this Part to the screenwriter of a cinematograph film\nfor which 2 or more individuals were involved in the writing of the\nscript or screenplay is a reference to the principal screenwriter.\nNote:\nIf there were 2 or more principal directors, 2 or more individuals who\nwere the principal producers, or 2 or more principal screenwriters, of a\ncinematograph film, section 195AZJ, 195AZK or 195AZL applies.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-191-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-191-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-191-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-191-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2793ac46fcb69d24e6e122543c20c507b15c8667eea70df203e3cb11474de5bf"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-191",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "191 Director, producer and screenwriter of cinematograph film",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A reference in this Part to the director of a cinematograph film in\nthe direction of which 2 or more individuals were involved is a\nreference to the principal director of the film and does not include a\nreference to any subsidiary director, whether described as an\nassociate director, line director, assistant director or in any other\nway.\n\n(2) A reference in this Part to the producer of a cinematograph film is\na reference to:\n\n(a) the individual who was the producer of the film; or\n\n(b) if there were 2 or more individuals involved in the production\nof the film—the individual who was the principal producer of\nthe film;\nand does not include a reference to any subsidiary producer,\nwhether described as an executive producer, associate producer,\nline producer, assistant producer or in any other way.\n\nSchedule 1  Moral rights of authors\n\n(3) As only individuals have moral rights (see section 190), if the\nproducer of a cinematograph film was a body corporate, the only\nmoral rights in respect of the film are those of the director and\nscreenwriter.\n\n(4) A reference in this Part to the screenwriter of a cinematograph film\nfor which 2 or more individuals were involved in the writing of the\nscript or screenplay is a reference to the principal screenwriter.\nNote:\nIf there were 2 or more principal directors, 2 or more individuals who\nwere the principal producers, or 2 or more principal screenwriters, of a\ncinematograph film, section 195AZJ, 195AZK or 195AZL applies."
    },
