    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "195 Nature of the identification of author",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the author of a work may be identified by\nany reasonable form of identification.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the author of a work has made known, either generally or to a\nperson who is required under this Part to identify the author,\nthat the author wishes to be identified in a particular way;\nand\n\n(b) the identification of the author in that way is reasonable in\nthe circumstances;\nthe identification is to be made in that way.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the author of a work may be identified by\nany reasonable form of identification.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the author of a work has made known, either generally or to a\nperson who is required under this Part to identify the author,\nthat the author wishes to be identified in a particular way;\nand\n\n(b) the identification of the author in that way is reasonable in\nthe circumstances;\nthe identification is to be made in that way.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6a0bb8676614588c39729248a417904d0cd1cc752b6275afca980c215cd17153"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "195 Nature of the identification of author",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the author of a work may be identified by\nany reasonable form of identification.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the author of a work has made known, either generally or to a\nperson who is required under this Part to identify the author,\nthat the author wishes to be identified in a particular way;\nand\n\n(b) the identification of the author in that way is reasonable in\nthe circumstances;\nthe identification is to be made in that way."
    },
