      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "When a literary, dramatic, musical or artistic work is reproduced in\na material form, an adaptation is made of a literary, dramatic or\nmusical work, or a copy of a cinematograph film is made, an\nidentification of the author is taken to be reasonably prominent if it\nis included on each reproduction of the work or of the adaptation or\non each copy of the film, as the case may be, in such a way that a\nperson acquiring the reproduction or copy will have notice of the\nauthor’s identity.\n\nSchedule 1  Moral rights of authors",
      "skos:definition": "When a literary, dramatic, musical or artistic work is reproduced in\na material form, an adaptation is made of a literary, dramatic or\nmusical work, or a copy of a cinematograph film is made, an\nidentification of the author is taken to be reasonably prominent if it\nis included on each reproduction of the work or of the adaptation or\non each copy of the film, as the case may be, in such a way that a\nperson acquiring the reproduction or copy will have notice of the\nauthor’s identity.\n\nSchedule 1  Moral rights of authors",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195ab-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195ab-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "61c8bf74affc8ff29e17f5a1bb512160c34fe5372bb95ad45dcbc86ad007fc03",
      "skos:note": "Identification of author's identity must be reasonably prominent in reproductions or copies."
    },
    {
