    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195af",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "195AF Acts of false attribution of authorship of cinematograph film",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195af"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the work is a cinematograph film.\n\n(2) It is an act of false attribution in relation to the director, producer\nor screenwriter of the film:\n\n(a) to insert or affix, or to authorise the inserting or affixing of, a\nperson’s name on the film or on a copy of the film in such a\nway as to imply falsely that the person is the director,\nproducer or screenwriter, as the case may be, of the film; or\n\n(b) to deal with the film or a copy of the film if a person’s name\nhas been so inserted or affixed on the film or a copy, as the\ncase may be, and the attributor knows that the person is not\nthe director, producer or screenwriter, as the case may be, of\nthe film; or\n\n(c) to transmit the film as being a film of which a person is the\ndirector, producer or screenwriter, as the case may be, if the\nattributor knows that the person is not the director, producer\nor screenwriter of the film.\n\nSchedule 1  Moral rights of authors",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if the work is a cinematograph film.\n\n(2) It is an act of false attribution in relation to the director, producer\nor screenwriter of the film:\n\n(a) to insert or affix, or to authorise the inserting or affixing of, a\nperson’s name on the film or on a copy of the film in such a\nway as to imply falsely that the person is the director,\nproducer or screenwriter, as the case may be, of the film; or\n\n(b) to deal with the film or a copy of the film if a person’s name\nhas been so inserted or affixed on the film or a copy, as the\ncase may be, and the attributor knows that the person is not\nthe director, producer or screenwriter, as the case may be, of\nthe film; or\n\n(c) to transmit the film as being a film of which a person is the\ndirector, producer or screenwriter, as the case may be, if the\nattributor knows that the person is not the director, producer\nor screenwriter of the film.\n\nSchedule 1  Moral rights of authors",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195af-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195af-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bf99f9aeff2594152f33d2482d5e028156e9bf80221c4949d3d26167aeb1c91c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195af",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "195AF Acts of false attribution of authorship of cinematograph film",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the work is a cinematograph film.\n\n(2) It is an act of false attribution in relation to the director, producer\nor screenwriter of the film:\n\n(a) to insert or affix, or to authorise the inserting or affixing of, a\nperson’s name on the film or on a copy of the film in such a\nway as to imply falsely that the person is the director,\nproducer or screenwriter, as the case may be, of the film; or\n\n(b) to deal with the film or a copy of the film if a person’s name\nhas been so inserted or affixed on the film or a copy, as the\ncase may be, and the attributor knows that the person is not\nthe director, producer or screenwriter, as the case may be, of\nthe film; or\n\n(c) to transmit the film as being a film of which a person is the\ndirector, producer or screenwriter, as the case may be, if the\nattributor knows that the person is not the director, producer\nor screenwriter of the film.\n\nSchedule 1  Moral rights of authors"
    },
