    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195ag",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "195AG Acts of false attribution of authorship of altered literary,",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195ag"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "dramatic, musical or artistic work\n\n(1) If the work is a literary, dramatic, musical or artistic work that has\nbeen altered by a person other than the author of the work, it is an\nact of false attribution in relation to the author of the work:\n\n(a) to deal with the work as so altered, as being the unaltered\nwork of the author; or\n\n(b) to deal with a reproduction of the work as so altered, as being\na reproduction of the unaltered work of the author;\nif, to the knowledge of the attributor, it is not the unaltered work or\na reproduction of the unaltered work, as the case may be, of the\nauthor.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the effect of the alteration is insubstantial; or\n\n(b) the alteration was required by law to be made, or was\notherwise necessary to avoid a breach of any law.",
      "skos:definition": "dramatic, musical or artistic work\n\n(1) If the work is a literary, dramatic, musical or artistic work that has\nbeen altered by a person other than the author of the work, it is an\nact of false attribution in relation to the author of the work:\n\n(a) to deal with the work as so altered, as being the unaltered\nwork of the author; or\n\n(b) to deal with a reproduction of the work as so altered, as being\na reproduction of the unaltered work of the author;\nif, to the knowledge of the attributor, it is not the unaltered work or\na reproduction of the unaltered work, as the case may be, of the\nauthor.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the effect of the alteration is insubstantial; or\n\n(b) the alteration was required by law to be made, or was\notherwise necessary to avoid a breach of any law.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195ag-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195ag-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "055bab7702b44d6f9fe72470a2f5245772a2baf4e582b6a44ca7265c29aa2b19"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195ag",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "195AG Acts of false attribution of authorship of altered literary,",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "dramatic, musical or artistic work\n\n(1) If the work is a literary, dramatic, musical or artistic work that has\nbeen altered by a person other than the author of the work, it is an\nact of false attribution in relation to the author of the work:\n\n(a) to deal with the work as so altered, as being the unaltered\nwork of the author; or\n\n(b) to deal with a reproduction of the work as so altered, as being\na reproduction of the unaltered work of the author;\nif, to the knowledge of the attributor, it is not the unaltered work or\na reproduction of the unaltered work, as the case may be, of the\nauthor.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the effect of the alteration is insubstantial; or\n\n(b) the alteration was required by law to be made, or was\notherwise necessary to avoid a breach of any law."
    },
    {
