    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195an",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "195AN Exercise of moral rights",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195an"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the author of a work dies, the author’s moral rights (other than\nthe right of integrity of authorship in respect of a cinematograph\nfilm) in respect of the work may be exercised and enforced by his\nor her legal personal representative.\n\n(2) If the affairs of the author of a work are lawfully administered by\nanother person (except under a law for the relief of bankrupt or\n\nMoral rights of authors  Schedule 1\n\ninsolvent debtors), the author’s moral rights may be exercised and\nenforced by the person administering his or her affairs.\n\n(3) Subject to this section, a moral right in respect of a work is not\ntransmissible by assignment, by will, or by devolution by operation\nof law.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) a cinematograph film; or\n\n(b) a literary, dramatic, musical or artistic work as included in a\ncinematograph film;\nhas 2 or more authors, the authors may enter into a written\nco-authorship agreement by which each of them agrees not to\nexercise his or her right of integrity of authorship in respect of the\nfilm or work, as the case may be, except jointly with the other\nauthor or authors.\n\n(5) A co-authorship agreement has effect according to its terms.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the author of a work dies, the author’s moral rights (other than\nthe right of integrity of authorship in respect of a cinematograph\nfilm) in respect of the work may be exercised and enforced by his\nor her legal personal representative.\n\n(2) If the affairs of the author of a work are lawfully administered by\nanother person (except under a law for the relief of bankrupt or\n\nMoral rights of authors  Schedule 1\n\ninsolvent debtors), the author’s moral rights may be exercised and\nenforced by the person administering his or her affairs.\n\n(3) Subject to this section, a moral right in respect of a work is not\ntransmissible by assignment, by will, or by devolution by operation\nof law.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) a cinematograph film; or\n\n(b) a literary, dramatic, musical or artistic work as included in a\ncinematograph film;\nhas 2 or more authors, the authors may enter into a written\nco-authorship agreement by which each of them agrees not to\nexercise his or her right of integrity of authorship in respect of the\nfilm or work, as the case may be, except jointly with the other\nauthor or authors.\n\n(5) A co-authorship agreement has effect according to its terms.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195an-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195an-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195an-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195an-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195an-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e48b96b5c42501b253c5c668495f7328a44f65d224d88294b0bde8ea6241bbff"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195an",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "195AN Exercise of moral rights",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the author of a work dies, the author’s moral rights (other than\nthe right of integrity of authorship in respect of a cinematograph\nfilm) in respect of the work may be exercised and enforced by his\nor her legal personal representative.\n\n(2) If the affairs of the author of a work are lawfully administered by\nanother person (except under a law for the relief of bankrupt or\n\nMoral rights of authors  Schedule 1\n\ninsolvent debtors), the author’s moral rights may be exercised and\nenforced by the person administering his or her affairs.\n\n(3) Subject to this section, a moral right in respect of a work is not\ntransmissible by assignment, by will, or by devolution by operation\nof law.\n\n(4) If:\n\n(a) a cinematograph film; or\n\n(b) a literary, dramatic, musical or artistic work as included in a\ncinematograph film;\nhas 2 or more authors, the authors may enter into a written\nco-authorship agreement by which each of them agrees not to\nexercise his or her right of integrity of authorship in respect of the\nfilm or work, as the case may be, except jointly with the other\nauthor or authors.\n\n(5) A co-authorship agreement has effect according to its terms."
    },
