      },
      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person does not, by subjecting a work, or authorising a work to\nbe subjected, to derogatory treatment, infringe the author’s right of\nintegrity of authorship in respect of the work if the person\nestablishes that it was reasonable in all the circumstances to subject\nthe work to the treatment.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person does not, by subjecting a work, or authorising a work to\nbe subjected, to derogatory treatment, infringe the author’s right of\nintegrity of authorship in respect of the work if the person\nestablishes that it was reasonable in all the circumstances to subject\nthe work to the treatment.",
      "values:partOf": {
