      "cml:premiseText": "Reasonable treatment"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195as-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "195AS(2) No infringement of right of integrity of authorship if",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195as-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The matters to be taken into account in determining for the\npurposes of subsection (1) whether it was reasonable in particular\ncircumstances to subject a literary, dramatic, musical or artistic\nwork to derogatory treatment include the following:\n\n(a) the nature of the work;\n\n(b) the purpose for which the work is used;\n\n(c) the manner in which the work is used;\n\n(d) the context in which the work is used;\n\n(e) any practice, in the industry in which the work is used, that is\nrelevant to the work or the use of the work;\n\n(f) any practice contained in a voluntary code of practice, in the\nindustry in which the work is used, that is relevant to the\nwork or the use of the work;\n\n(g) whether the work was made:\n\n(i) in the course of the author’s employment; or\n\n(ii) under a contract for the performance by the author of\nservices for another person;\n\n(h) whether the treatment was required by law or was otherwise\nnecessary to avoid a breach of any law;\n\nMoral rights of authors  Schedule 1\n\n(i) if the work has 2 or more authors—their views about the\ntreatment.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The matters to be taken into account in determining for the\npurposes of subsection (1) whether it was reasonable in particular\ncircumstances to subject a literary, dramatic, musical or artistic\nwork to derogatory treatment include the following:\n\n(a) the nature of the work;\n\n(b) the purpose for which the work is used;\n\n(c) the manner in which the work is used;\n\n(d) the context in which the work is used;\n\n(e) any practice, in the industry in which the work is used, that is\nrelevant to the work or the use of the work;\n\n(f) any practice contained in a voluntary code of practice, in the\nindustry in which the work is used, that is relevant to the\nwork or the use of the work;\n\n(g) whether the work was made:\n\n(i) in the course of the author’s employment; or\n\n(ii) under a contract for the performance by the author of\nservices for another person;\n\n(h) whether the treatment was required by law or was otherwise\nnecessary to avoid a breach of any law;\n\nMoral rights of authors  Schedule 1\n\n(i) if the work has 2 or more authors—their views about the\ntreatment.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195as"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195as-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195as-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
