    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195as-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "195AS(3) No infringement of right of integrity of authorship if",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195as-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The matters to be taken into account in determining for the\npurposes of subsection (1) whether it was reasonable in particular\ncircumstances to subject a cinematograph film to derogatory\ntreatment include the following:\n\n(a) the nature of the film;\n\n(b) whether the primary purpose for which the film was made\nwas for exhibition at cinemas, for broadcasting by television\nor for some other use;\n\n(c) the purpose for which the film is used;\n\n(d) the manner in which the film is used;\n\n(e) the context in which the film is used;\n\n(f) any practice, in the industry in which the film is used, that is\nrelevant to the film or the use of the film;\n\n(g) any practice contained in a voluntary code of practice, in the\nindustry in which the film is used, that is relevant to the film\nor the use of the film;\n\n(h) whether the film was made in the course of the employment\nof the director, producer or screenwriter who alleges that the\ntreatment was derogatory;\n\n(i) whether the treatment was required by law or was otherwise\nnecessary to avoid a breach of any law.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The matters to be taken into account in determining for the\npurposes of subsection (1) whether it was reasonable in particular\ncircumstances to subject a cinematograph film to derogatory\ntreatment include the following:\n\n(a) the nature of the film;\n\n(b) whether the primary purpose for which the film was made\nwas for exhibition at cinemas, for broadcasting by television\nor for some other use;\n\n(c) the purpose for which the film is used;\n\n(d) the manner in which the film is used;\n\n(e) the context in which the film is used;\n\n(f) any practice, in the industry in which the film is used, that is\nrelevant to the film or the use of the film;\n\n(g) any practice contained in a voluntary code of practice, in the\nindustry in which the film is used, that is relevant to the film\nor the use of the film;\n\n(h) whether the film was made in the course of the employment\nof the director, producer or screenwriter who alleges that the\ntreatment was derogatory;\n\n(i) whether the treatment was required by law or was otherwise\nnecessary to avoid a breach of any law.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195as"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195as-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195as-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195as-ss-3-logic-argumentation-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1a93e46aca04bd0e4f1b513e5d3bada5769fd3c38ee40adeb5e6c918dd2c4816",
      "skos:note": "Matters to be considered when determining reasonableness of derogatory treatment in a film."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195as-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "195AS(3) No infringement of right of integrity of authorship if",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The matters to be taken into account in determining for the\npurposes of subsection (1) whether it was reasonable in particular\ncircumstances to subject a cinematograph film to derogatory\ntreatment include the following:\n\n(a) the nature of the film;\n\n(b) whether the primary purpose for which the film was made\nwas for exhibition at cinemas, for broadcasting by television\nor for some other use;\n\n(c) the purpose for which the film is used;\n\n(d) the manner in which the film is used;\n\n(e) the context in which the film is used;\n\n(f) any practice, in the industry in which the film is used, that is\nrelevant to the film or the use of the film;\n\n(g) any practice contained in a voluntary code of practice, in the\nindustry in which the film is used, that is relevant to the film\nor the use of the film;\n\n(h) whether the film was made in the course of the employment\nof the director, producer or screenwriter who alleges that the\ntreatment was derogatory;\n\n(i) whether the treatment was required by law or was otherwise\nnecessary to avoid a breach of any law."
    },
