      },
      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A person who does any act referred to in subsection 195AQ(3), (4)\nor (5) in respect of a work that has been subjected to derogatory\ntreatment of a kind mentioned in that subsection does not, by doing\nthat act, infringe the author’s right of integrity of authorship in\nrespect of the work if the person establishes that it was reasonable\nin all the circumstances to do that act.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A person who does any act referred to in subsection 195AQ(3), (4)\nor (5) in respect of a work that has been subjected to derogatory\ntreatment of a kind mentioned in that subsection does not, by doing\nthat act, infringe the author’s right of integrity of authorship in\nrespect of the work if the person establishes that it was reasonable\nin all the circumstances to do that act.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195as"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
