    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195at-ss-4a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "195AT(4A) Certain treatment of works not to constitute an infringement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195at-ss-4a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "(4A) The removal or relocation by a person (the remover) of a moveable\nartistic work that is situated at a place that is accessible to the\npublic, and was made for installation in that place, is not an\ninfringement of the author’s right of integrity of authorship in\nrespect of the work if the remover:\n\n(a) after making reasonable inquiries, cannot discover the\nidentity and location of the author or a person representing\nthe author; or\n\n(b) if paragraph (a) does not apply—complies with\nsubsection (4B) in relation to the removal or relocation.",
      "skos:definition": "(4A) The removal or relocation by a person (the remover) of a moveable\nartistic work that is situated at a place that is accessible to the\npublic, and was made for installation in that place, is not an\ninfringement of the author’s right of integrity of authorship in\nrespect of the work if the remover:\n\n(a) after making reasonable inquiries, cannot discover the\nidentity and location of the author or a person representing\nthe author; or\n\n(b) if paragraph (a) does not apply—complies with\nsubsection (4B) in relation to the removal or relocation.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195at"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195at-ss-4a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195at-ss-4a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9f03a3271e128c017975205f715ab2f38d06405c4bbd386f215efb771be40aad",
      "skos:note": "Removal or relocation of a work not an infringement if certain conditions met"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195at-ss-4a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "195AT(4A) Certain treatment of works not to constitute an infringement",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 21,
      "values:originalText": "(4A) The removal or relocation by a person (the remover) of a moveable\nartistic work that is situated at a place that is accessible to the\npublic, and was made for installation in that place, is not an\ninfringement of the author’s right of integrity of authorship in\nrespect of the work if the remover:\n\n(a) after making reasonable inquiries, cannot discover the\nidentity and location of the author or a person representing\nthe author; or\n\n(b) if paragraph (a) does not apply—complies with\nsubsection (4B) in relation to the removal or relocation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195at-ss-4a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195at-ss-4a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195at-ss-4a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to comply with subsection (4B)",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Remover must comply with subsection (4B)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "No infringement"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195at-ss-4b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "195AT(4B) Certain treatment of works not to constitute an infringement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195at-ss-4b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "(4B) This subsection is complied with by the remover in relation to the\nremoval or relocation of a moveable artistic work if:\n\n(a) the remover has, in accordance with the regulations and\nbefore the removal or relocation is carried out, given the\nauthor or a person representing the author a written notice\nstating the remover’s intention to carry out the removal or\nrelocation; and\n\n(b) the notice stated that the person to whom the notice was\ngiven may, within 3 weeks from the date of the notice, seek\nto have access to the work for either or both of the following\npurposes:\n\n(i) making a record of the work;\n\n(ii) consulting in good faith with the remover about the\nremoval or relocation; and\n\n(c) the notice contained such other information and particulars as\nare prescribed; and\n\n(d) where the person to whom the notice was given notifies the\nremover within the period of 3 weeks referred to in\nparagraph (b) that the person wishes to have access to the\nwork for either or both of the purposes mentioned in that\nparagraph—the remover has given the person a reasonable\nopportunity within a further period of 3 weeks to have such\naccess; and\n\nMoral rights of authors  Schedule 1\n\n(e) where the person to whom the notice was given notifies the\nremover that the person requires the removal from the work\nof the author’s identification as the author of the work—the\nremover has complied with the requirement.",
      "skos:definition": "(4B) This subsection is complied with by the remover in relation to the\nremoval or relocation of a moveable artistic work if:\n\n(a) the remover has, in accordance with the regulations and\nbefore the removal or relocation is carried out, given the\nauthor or a person representing the author a written notice\nstating the remover’s intention to carry out the removal or\nrelocation; and\n\n(b) the notice stated that the person to whom the notice was\ngiven may, within 3 weeks from the date of the notice, seek\nto have access to the work for either or both of the following\npurposes:\n\n(i) making a record of the work;\n\n(ii) consulting in good faith with the remover about the\nremoval or relocation; and\n\n(c) the notice contained such other information and particulars as\nare prescribed; and\n\n(d) where the person to whom the notice was given notifies the\nremover within the period of 3 weeks referred to in\nparagraph (b) that the person wishes to have access to the\nwork for either or both of the purposes mentioned in that\nparagraph—the remover has given the person a reasonable\nopportunity within a further period of 3 weeks to have such\naccess; and\n\nMoral rights of authors  Schedule 1\n\n(e) where the person to whom the notice was given notifies the\nremover that the person requires the removal from the work\nof the author’s identification as the author of the work—the\nremover has complied with the requirement.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195at"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195at-ss-4b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195at-ss-4b-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195at-ss-4b-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195at-ss-4b-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195at-ss-4b-logic-epistemic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195at-ss-4b-logic-ltl-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1568da8f7e73da2904fdc2a1db3b6ae48a849e225752a31ced0c6d2e725e9a6b",
      "skos:note": "Remover must give notice to author before removal or relocation of artistic work.",
      "dc:description": "written notice stating intention to carry out removal or relocation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195at-ss-4b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "195AT(4B) Certain treatment of works not to constitute an infringement",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 21,
      "values:originalText": "(4B) This subsection is complied with by the remover in relation to the\nremoval or relocation of a moveable artistic work if:\n\n(a) the remover has, in accordance with the regulations and\nbefore the removal or relocation is carried out, given the\nauthor or a person representing the author a written notice\nstating the remover’s intention to carry out the removal or\nrelocation; and\n\n(b) the notice stated that the person to whom the notice was\ngiven may, within 3 weeks from the date of the notice, seek\nto have access to the work for either or both of the following\npurposes:\n\n(i) making a record of the work;\n\n(ii) consulting in good faith with the remover about the\nremoval or relocation; and\n\n(c) the notice contained such other information and particulars as\nare prescribed; and\n\n(d) where the person to whom the notice was given notifies the\nremover within the period of 3 weeks referred to in\nparagraph (b) that the person wishes to have access to the\nwork for either or both of the purposes mentioned in that\nparagraph—the remover has given the person a reasonable\nopportunity within a further period of 3 weeks to have such\naccess; and\n\nMoral rights of authors  Schedule 1\n\n(e) where the person to whom the notice was given notifies the\nremover that the person requires the removal from the work\nof the author’s identification as the author of the work—the\nremover has complied with the requirement."
    },
