    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195aw-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "195AW(2) Author’s consent to act or omission—films or works in films",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195aw-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If:\n\n(a) a person makes a statement to another person; and\n\n(b) the person makes the statement knowing:\n\nSchedule 1  Moral rights of authors\n\n(i) that the statement is false or misleading in a material\nparticular; or\n\n(ii) that a matter or thing has been omitted from the\nstatement without which the statement is false or\nmisleading in a material particular; and\n\n(c) the person makes the statement with the intention of\npersuading the other person to give, or not to give, a consent\nfor the purposes of section 195AW or 195AWA;\nthe consent does not have any effect.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If:\n\n(a) a person makes a statement to another person; and\n\n(b) the person makes the statement knowing:\n\nSchedule 1  Moral rights of authors\n\n(i) that the statement is false or misleading in a material\nparticular; or\n\n(ii) that a matter or thing has been omitted from the\nstatement without which the statement is false or\nmisleading in a material particular; and\n\n(c) the person makes the statement with the intention of\npersuading the other person to give, or not to give, a consent\nfor the purposes of section 195AW or 195AWA;\nthe consent does not have any effect.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195aw"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195aw-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195aw-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195aw-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "230e7e49053000d88bfc6c600fb96fd16e4c29dc2c03b72d49ff5bebb60c2fec",
      "skos:note": "Consent to act or omission—films or works in films Consent may be given in relation to all or any acts or omissions occurring before or after the consent is given. Written consent is required for acts or omissions affecting an author's moral right."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195aw-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "195AW(2) Author’s consent to act or omission—films or works in films",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If:\n\n(a) a person makes a statement to another person; and\n\n(b) the person makes the statement knowing:\n\nSchedule 1  Moral rights of authors\n\n(i) that the statement is false or misleading in a material\nparticular; or\n\n(ii) that a matter or thing has been omitted from the\nstatement without which the statement is false or\nmisleading in a material particular; and\n\n(c) the person makes the statement with the intention of\npersuading the other person to give, or not to give, a consent\nfor the purposes of section 195AW or 195AWA;\nthe consent does not have any effect."
    },
