        "@id": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to section 203, the relief that a court may grant in an action\nfor an infringement of any of an author’s moral rights in respect of\na work includes any one or more of the following:\n\n(a) an injunction (subject to any terms that the court thinks fit);\n\nMoral rights of authors  Schedule 1\n\n(b) damages for loss resulting from the infringement;\n\n(c) a declaration that a moral right of the author has been\ninfringed;\n\n(d) an order that the defendant make a public apology for the\ninfringement;\n\n(e) an order that any false attribution of authorship, or\nderogatory treatment, of the work be removed or reversed.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to section 203, the relief that a court may grant in an action\nfor an infringement of any of an author’s moral rights in respect of\na work includes any one or more of the following:\n\n(a) an injunction (subject to any terms that the court thinks fit);\n\nMoral rights of authors  Schedule 1\n\n(b) damages for loss resulting from the infringement;\n\n(c) a declaration that a moral right of the author has been\ninfringed;\n\n(d) an order that the defendant make a public apology for the\ninfringement;\n\n(e) an order that any false attribution of authorship, or\nderogatory treatment, of the work be removed or reversed.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-1-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-1-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-1-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-1-logic-descriptionlogic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0663cff9ea8f9afdbc52567e891787d6d5d8b8e46251935852b7ab04f38343ff",
      "skos:note": "Jurisdiction of the Supreme Court in a matter arising under this Part is to be exercised by a single Judge. No effect on other remedies in proceedings under this Part Section 127 applies in respect of an action brought under this Part. Court may grant injunctions, damages, declaration, apology, or removal of false attribution in moral rights infringement action."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195az-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "195AZ(1) Actions for infringement of moral rights",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to section 203, the relief that a court may grant in an action\nfor an infringement of any of an author’s moral rights in respect of\na work includes any one or more of the following:\n\n(a) an injunction (subject to any terms that the court thinks fit);\n\nMoral rights of authors  Schedule 1\n\n(b) damages for loss resulting from the infringement;\n\n(c) a declaration that a moral right of the author has been\ninfringed;\n\n(d) an order that the defendant make a public apology for the\ninfringement;\n\n(e) an order that any false attribution of authorship, or\nderogatory treatment, of the work be removed or reversed."
    },
