    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "195AZ(2) Actions for infringement of moral rights",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195az-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(2) In exercising its discretion as to the appropriate relief to be granted,\nthe court may take into account any of the following:\n\n(a) whether the defendant was aware, or ought reasonably to\nhave been aware, of the author’s moral rights;\n\n(b) the effect on the author’s honour or reputation resulting from\nany damage to the work;\n\n(c) the number, and categories, of people who have seen or heard\nthe work;\n\n(d) anything done by the defendant to mitigate the effects of the\ninfringement;\n\n(e) if the moral right that was infringed was a right of attribution\nof authorship—any cost or difficulty that would have been\nassociated with identifying the author;\n\n(f) any cost or difficulty in removing or reversing any false\nattribution of authorship, or derogatory treatment, of the\nwork.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) In exercising its discretion as to the appropriate relief to be granted,\nthe court may take into account any of the following:\n\n(a) whether the defendant was aware, or ought reasonably to\nhave been aware, of the author’s moral rights;\n\n(b) the effect on the author’s honour or reputation resulting from\nany damage to the work;\n\n(c) the number, and categories, of people who have seen or heard\nthe work;\n\n(d) anything done by the defendant to mitigate the effects of the\ninfringement;\n\n(e) if the moral right that was infringed was a right of attribution\nof authorship—any cost or difficulty that would have been\nassociated with identifying the author;\n\n(f) any cost or difficulty in removing or reversing any false\nattribution of authorship, or derogatory treatment, of the\nwork.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-2-logic-deontic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3cc59b91ceef452fb2acd4b2c987b141e0f7e281c2c63b22c79418d4ad00e059",
      "skos:note": "Court may consider factors when granting relief for moral rights infringement. Damages recovered in one proceeding are taken into account in assessing damages in another proceeding arising out of the same operation or transaction. Decision of a court is final. Presumption of authorship for film director, producer or screenwriter"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195az-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "195AZ(2) Actions for infringement of moral rights",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(2) In exercising its discretion as to the appropriate relief to be granted,\nthe court may take into account any of the following:\n\n(a) whether the defendant was aware, or ought reasonably to\nhave been aware, of the author’s moral rights;\n\n(b) the effect on the author’s honour or reputation resulting from\nany damage to the work;\n\n(c) the number, and categories, of people who have seen or heard\nthe work;\n\n(d) anything done by the defendant to mitigate the effects of the\ninfringement;\n\n(e) if the moral right that was infringed was a right of attribution\nof authorship—any cost or difficulty that would have been\nassociated with identifying the author;\n\n(f) any cost or difficulty in removing or reversing any false\nattribution of authorship, or derogatory treatment, of the\nwork."
    },
