    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-3-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to consider negotiating a settlement.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Court must decide whether to grant an injunction.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Negotiating a settlement is required before granting an injunction."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": ">=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Court must adjourn hearing for negotiation period.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Court has the power to adjourn hearings.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Adjournment is required for negotiation period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "195AZ(4) Actions for infringement of moral rights",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195az-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n\n(a) the work is a cinematograph film; and\n\n(b) the action is brought by a person who is a screenwriter of the\nfilm; and\n\n(c) the relief granted in the action consists of or includes\ndamages; and\n\n(d) the person has already been granted relief by way of damages\nin an action for an infringement of his or her moral rights as\n\nSchedule 1  Moral rights of authors\n\nan author of the dramatic work constituted by the script or\nscreenplay for the film;\nthe amount of any damages that, apart from this subsection, would\nbe awarded to the person in the action referred to in paragraph (b)\nis to be reduced by the amount of the damages awarded to the\nperson in the action referred to in paragraph (d).",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If:\n\n(a) the work is a cinematograph film; and\n\n(b) the action is brought by a person who is a screenwriter of the\nfilm; and\n\n(c) the relief granted in the action consists of or includes\ndamages; and\n\n(d) the person has already been granted relief by way of damages\nin an action for an infringement of his or her moral rights as\n\nSchedule 1  Moral rights of authors\n\nan author of the dramatic work constituted by the script or\nscreenplay for the film;\nthe amount of any damages that, apart from this subsection, would\nbe awarded to the person in the action referred to in paragraph (b)\nis to be reduced by the amount of the damages awarded to the\nperson in the action referred to in paragraph (d).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-4-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-4-logic-descriptionlogic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ca81b3a294bbfb49cae2a15b814b67476b07f747da74e2a1a8655565e2e47d39",
      "skos:note": "Federal Court of Australia has jurisdiction over matters arising under this Part. Reduction of damages for screenwriters in moral rights infringement actions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195az-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "195AZ(4) Actions for infringement of moral rights",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n\n(a) the work is a cinematograph film; and\n\n(b) the action is brought by a person who is a screenwriter of the\nfilm; and\n\n(c) the relief granted in the action consists of or includes\ndamages; and\n\n(d) the person has already been granted relief by way of damages\nin an action for an infringement of his or her moral rights as\n\nSchedule 1  Moral rights of authors\n\nan author of the dramatic work constituted by the script or\nscreenplay for the film;\nthe amount of any damages that, apart from this subsection, would\nbe awarded to the person in the action referred to in paragraph (b)\nis to be reduced by the amount of the damages awarded to the\nperson in the action referred to in paragraph (d)."
    },
