    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "195AZ(4) Actions for infringement of moral rights",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195az-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Federal Court of Australia has jurisdiction with respect to\nmatters arising under this Part.\n195AZD  Presumption as to subsistence of copyright\n\nIn an action brought under this Part for an infringement of a moral\nright in respect of a work, copyright is presumed to subsist in the\nwork if the defendant does not put in issue the question whether\ncopyright subsists in the work.\n195AZE  Presumption as to subsistence of moral rights\n\nIn an action brought under this Part for an infringement of a moral\nright in respect of a work, if copyright is presumed or proved to\nhave subsisted in the work when the infringement is alleged to\nhave occurred, the moral right is presumed to have subsisted in the\nwork at that time.\n195AZF  Presumptions in relation to authorship of work",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The Federal Court of Australia has jurisdiction with respect to\nmatters arising under this Part.\n195AZD  Presumption as to subsistence of copyright\n\nIn an action brought under this Part for an infringement of a moral\nright in respect of a work, copyright is presumed to subsist in the\nwork if the defendant does not put in issue the question whether\ncopyright subsists in the work.\n195AZE  Presumption as to subsistence of moral rights\n\nIn an action brought under this Part for an infringement of a moral\nright in respect of a work, if copyright is presumed or proved to\nhave subsisted in the work when the infringement is alleged to\nhave occurred, the moral right is presumed to have subsisted in the\nwork at that time.\n195AZF  Presumptions in relation to authorship of work",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-4-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-4-logic-descriptionlogic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5707faa27a02291be78c349d44318c7f653c79cbc93648155543dfda0d5ff71c",
      "skos:note": "Federal Court of Australia has jurisdiction over matters arising under this Part. Reduction of damages for screenwriters in moral rights infringement actions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195az-ss-4",
