    {
      "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "195AZ(2) Actions for infringement of moral rights",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195az-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If a name purporting to be the name of the director, producer or\nscreenwriter of a cinematograph film appeared on copies of the\nfilm that were issued when the film was made, then, in an action\n\nSchedule 1  Moral rights of authors\n\nbrought under this Part, the person whose name so appeared is, if it\nwas his or her true name or a name by which he or she was\ncommonly known, presumed, unless the contrary is established, to\nbe the director, producer or screenwriter, as the case may be, of the\nfilm.\n195AZG  Other presumptions in relation to literary, dramatic,\nmusical or artistic work\n\nSections 128 and 129 apply in respect of an action brought under\nthis Part.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If a name purporting to be the name of the director, producer or\nscreenwriter of a cinematograph film appeared on copies of the\nfilm that were issued when the film was made, then, in an action\n\nSchedule 1  Moral rights of authors\n\nbrought under this Part, the person whose name so appeared is, if it\nwas his or her true name or a name by which he or she was\ncommonly known, presumed, unless the contrary is established, to\nbe the director, producer or screenwriter, as the case may be, of the\nfilm.\n195AZG  Other presumptions in relation to literary, dramatic,\nmusical or artistic work\n\nSections 128 and 129 apply in respect of an action brought under\nthis Part.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000-sch-1-sec-195az-ss-2-logic-deontic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bca6fa706b1479a26d87d7350d9041cbaa194a5c50d57f072ac893ed80b117c0",
      "skos:note": "Court may consider factors when granting relief for moral rights infringement. Damages recovered in one proceeding are taken into account in assessing damages in another proceeding arising out of the same operation or transaction. Decision of a court is final. Presumption of authorship for film director, producer or screenwriter"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/copyright-amendment-moral-rights-act-2000#sch-1-sec-195az-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "195AZ(2) Actions for infringement of moral rights",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If a name purporting to be the name of the director, producer or\nscreenwriter of a cinematograph film appeared on copies of the\nfilm that were issued when the film was made, then, in an action\n\nSchedule 1  Moral rights of authors\n\nbrought under this Part, the person whose name so appeared is, if it\nwas his or her true name or a name by which he or she was\ncommonly known, presumed, unless the contrary is established, to\nbe the director, producer or screenwriter, as the case may be, of the\nfilm.\n195AZG  Other presumptions in relation to literary, dramatic,\nmusical or artistic work\n\nSections 128 and 129 apply in respect of an action brought under\nthis Part."
    },
    {
